<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brazilian Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Empire of Brazil</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Brazilian Empire was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitutional-monarchy">constitutional monarchy</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a> from 1822 to 1889, founded when Pedro, son of the Portuguese king, declared <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>'s independence and became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-i-of-brazil">Emperor Pedro I</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-ii-of-brazil">Pedro II</a> it achieved relative stability through a constitution that gave the emperor a moderating power. It ended in 1889 when the military overthrew the monarchy, the year after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> was abolished.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire.jpg" alt="Brazilian Empire" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This vector image includes elements that have been taken or adapted from this file · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Brazil_(1853-1889).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
